# `module::Field::loss`

[Back to `module::Field`](../Field.md)

The loss of the model prices against the quotes, as a rank-zero `Series`.

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series module::Field::loss(const pluss::Series &target_prices, pluss::Config cfg = {}) const;
```

## What It Does

Reduces the residuals to one number by the loss chosen in `controls.loss` ([`Loss`](../Loss.md): `MSE`, `RelativeMSE`, `MAE` or `Huber`, all means over the options with no weights). The result is a `Series`, so it can be differentiated or combined with other `Series` code; [`loss_value`](loss_value.md) returns the same number as a `double`.

## Parameters

`const pluss::Series &target_prices`
: One quote per option.

`pluss::Config cfg`
: Device.

## Returns

The loss as a rank-zero `Series`.

## Errors

- As for `residuals`; a non-positive `huber_delta` with the Huber loss throws.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The four losses of the same residuals.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.02}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  const Series prices = field.price().price;
  const Series quotes = prices + pluss::make_series({0.30, -0.20, 0.10, -0.40, 0.25});

  for (const mod::Loss loss : {mod::Loss::MSE, mod::Loss::RelativeMSE, mod::Loss::MAE, mod::Loss::Huber}) {
    field.controls.loss = loss;
    out.writeln(static_cast<int>(loss), ": loss =", field.loss(quotes).item<double>());
  }
}
```

### Example 2

The loss is a rank-zero `Series`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.02}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  const Series prices = field.price().price;
  const Series quotes = prices + pluss::make_series({0.30, -0.20, 0.10, -0.40, 0.25});

  const Series l = field.loss(quotes);
  out.writeln("rank =", l.dim(), ", value =", l.item<double>());
}
```

### Example 3

Reading a MSE by hand: the mean of the squared residuals.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(10));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.02}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  const Series prices = field.price().price;
  const Series quotes = prices + pluss::make_series({0.30, -0.20, 0.10, -0.40, 0.25});

  out.writeln("loss =", field.loss(quotes).item<double>(), ", mean(residual^2) =", field.residuals(quotes).square().mean().item<double>());
}
```

